# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of core.autocrlf.
# With core.autocrlf=true (Windows default), git would otherwise write CRLF
# into checked-out .sh files; a CRLF after the shebang (#!) causes the kernel
# exec to look for a binary named "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist — so
# docker-entrypoint.sh and healthcheck.sh would both fail with "no such file
# or directory" at container start.
*.sh text eol=lf
